      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a lot of duplicated code.\n\nAn alternative is to fill a temporary write buffer on the stack and pass into a common handler.\n\n`wr_buf[]` is currently 256 bytes, but I don\u0027t see any uses of `wr_buf_len` that exceed 8 bytes.\n\nThis could look like:\n```\nint rts54_post_command(*dev, cmd, *wr_buf, wr_len, *user_buf)\n    if (!IDLE)\n        return EBUSY;\n    k_mutex_lock();\n    if (data-\u003ecmd !\u003d NONE)\n        k_mutex_unlock();\n        return EBUSY;\n    \n    data-\u003ecmd \u003d cmd;\n    memcpy(data-\u003ewr_buf, wr_buf, wr_len);\n    data-\u003euser_buf \u003d user_buf;\n    \n    k_mutex_unlock()\n    k_sem_reset()\n    return 0;\n}\nint rts54_get_current_pdo(*dev, *pdo)\n    uint8_t wr_buf[4];\n   \n    wr_buf[0] \u003d GET_CURRENT_PARTNER_SRC_PDO.cmd;\n    ...\n    rts54_post_command(dev, CMD_GET_CURRENT_PARTNER_SRC_PDO, wr_buf...)\n```",
